# Legal acceptance version (must bump)

TourAI forces users to re-accept Terms/Privacy when the legal version changes. **Do not ship legal text edits without bumping the version.**

## Source of truth

Firestore document **`PublicConfig/Legal`**, field **`CurrentVersion`** (ISO date string, e.g. `2026-07-26`).

App and Web read this at runtime. An Android store release is **not** required only to bump this field.

## When this applies

Any edit to published legal content on this site, including:

- `terms.html`, `privacy.html`, `cookies.html`
- `js/locales/**` keys that embed legal page HTML (`page.terms.*`, `page.privacy.*`, …)
- `js/auth.js` legal re-acceptance / `LegalDocumentsVersion`

## Mandatory checklist (same calendar day as the legal change)

1. Set version strings to **today’s date** (`YYYY-MM-DD` from the session “Today’s date”).
2. Update **“Última actualización” / “Last updated”** in the edited legal HTML (es defaults + `en-GB.js`).
3. Align all of these to the **same** date string:
   - Firestore `PublicConfig/Legal.CurrentVersion` (tell the owner if you cannot write Firestore)
   - `js/auth.js` → `TourAiAuth.LegalDocumentsVersion` (and any local fallback)
   - App fallback `TourAI.Models/Policies/LegalAcceptancePolicy.FallbackVersion` when that repo is in scope
   - `TourAI/src/scripts/dataSeeds/PublicConfig_Legal.json` when in scope
4. In the reply to the owner, state clearly: **version bumped to `YYYY-MM-DD`** and whether Firestore still needs a manual update.

## Do not

- Change Terms/Privacy body and leave `CurrentVersion` unchanged
- Bump only Web and forget App fallback / Firestore
- Assume “continued use = acceptance” — re-acceptance is enforced in code
